From cc38855def58393a72cc7dfaa340e550efd9642a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GNB Build <palimpseste@quidam.eu>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 16:54:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] companion: WIFI home screen page with live radio on/off
 toggle

New DUAL_BLE_WIFI-only page (ui-new/UITask.cpp, alongside GPS/BLUETOOTH/
ADVERT), long-press toggles WiFi on/off immediately, no reboot -- same
pattern as the existing BLUETOOTH page (enableBluetooth/disableBluetooth
on MultiSerialInterface), but going one level deeper: SerialWifiInterface
enable()/disable() only gate the TCP servers own frame routing, not the
WiFi radio itself (unlike SerialBLEInterface, which really does start/
stop advertising in enable()/disable()). So UITask::toggleWiFi() drives
the radio directly (WiFi.begin()/disconnect()/mode()) plus interface_manager
add/removeInterface(), rather than reusing a shallow enable()/disable() call.

wifi_interface.begin() (the TCP server itself) now starts unconditionally,
exactly once, in main.cpp setup() regardless of wifi_enabled -- previously
only called when wifi_enabled was already set at boot. This lets the new
page turn WiFi on for the first time without ever re-calling begin() on
the server.

Page shows on/off state and, once connected, the IP address. Off state
also surfaces whether a SSID is configured yet, so a first-time user
knows to set wifi_ssid before expecting the toggle to do anything.

Compiled and verified on all 4 relevant envs (dual V4.3, dual Tracker V2,
plain BLE V4, plain WiFi V4) -- no regression on the untouched envs.
Not yet tested on real hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
